# --- Google OAuth (optional but recommended for the in-app popup) ---
# Create a "Web application" OAuth Client ID in Google Cloud Console and add
# your deployed origin (and http://localhost:3000) to "Authorized JavaScript origins".
# Without this, the app falls back to the shared sample client, which rejects
# unregistered origins with "400: origin_mismatch".
# Users can also paste their own Client ID directly in the sync dialog.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""

# --- Google Health / Google Fit (optional) ---
# Set to "true" only after you have:
#   1. enabled the Fitness API in Google Cloud Console for your OAuth client
#   2. added the Fitness scopes to the sign-in request
#      (https://www.googleapis.com/auth/fitness.activity.read,
#       fitness.body.read, fitness.sleep.read, fitness.heart_rate.read)
# When this flag is off (or the access token lacks the Fitness scopes), the
# Health dashboard still works and the "Sync with Google Health" button uses
# clearly-labelled simulated data.
VITE_GOOGLE_HEALTH_ENABLED=""

# --- Firebase (already provided by firebase-applet-config.json) ---
# Override only if you point the app at your own Firebase project.
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=""
